  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated Shelter and NFI Support for Displaced, Returnees, and Vulnerable Host Communities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtltbrgtThe proposed intervention aims to provide life-saving shelter and NFI support to vulnerable returnees, internally displaced persons (IDPs) and host communities in newly accessible areas of Ar-Raqqa (Sabka subdistrict -including Al-Shriedah town) and Basira subdistrict in Deir-ez-Zor, including (Al-Shihel and Sabha towns). The project will be implemented over a six-month period to improve living conditions, support safe returns, and enhance dignified temporary shelter solutions. To achieve this, the intervention will focus on private shelter repairs for partially damaged but structurally sound houses, enabling returnees to reinhabit their original homes. In parallel, the project will rehabilitate selected collective centers currently hosting IDPs in inadequate conditions, improving infrastructure, privacy, and access to basic WASH services. The intervention will be complemented by the distribution of core relief items (CRIs), including mattresses, blankets, kitchen sets, and other essential non-food items to both returnees and IDPs with unmet basic needs. Vulnerability-based targeting will prioritize female-headed households, persons with disabilities, and families lacking resources to meet their shelter and NFI needs. All activities will be carried out in coordination with local actors and aligned with SNFI sector standards. lt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
